            make_q("What is 'Mode Collapse' in Generative Adversarial Networks?", ["When the generator discovers a small handful of realistic samples that successfully fool the discriminator and produces only those few outputs, losing all dataset diversity", "When the GPU runs out of VRAM", "When the loss evaluates to negative infinity", "When the generator produces black images only"], 0, "Mode collapse occurs when the generator collapses onto a single narrow mode of the distribution (e.g. generating only one specific dog face repeatedly)."),
