            make_q("What are Diffusion Probabilistic Models (DDPM, Sohl-Dickstein 2015, Ho et al. 2020)?", ["Generative models that systematically add Gaussian noise in a forward process, and train a neural network to predict and remove noise step-by-step in a reverse process", "Models that simulate chemical gas diffusion", "Random walk models for stock prices", "Networks that diffuse heat across GPUs"], 0, "DDPMs formulate generation as a reverse Markov chain that iteratively denoises pure Gaussian noise into realistic data samples."),
